    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0308" n="190" xml:id="pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.5045/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Cape Haitien</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wood</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cape Haitien</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1929-12-04">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received
                        December 4, 1929—3:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Demonstration sympathetic with disturbance in Port-au-Prince has developed here,
                    mob numbering about one thousand parading. No violence as yet. May be necessary
                    to declare martial law.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
